## 7. ANIMATIONS & MICRO-INTERACTIONS

Use Framer Motion consistently.

Animation goals:
- Smooth and premium.
- Fast enough for a social network.
- Subtle rather than distracting.
- Consistent across every page.

Implement:
- Page transition fade and slight vertical movement.
- Staggered entrance for lists and community cards.
- Card hover lift of approximately 2–4px.
- Smooth color and border transitions.
- Button hover and pressed states.
- Animated sidebar collapse.
- Modal scale/fade entrance and exit.
- Dropdown entrance and exit.
- Expand/collapse comment threads.
- Toast slide-in and fade-out.
- Skeleton shimmer.
- Loading spinners.
- Tab indicator transitions.
- Heart reaction animation.
- Subtle orange glow around focused elements.
- Animated loading states for forms.

Use short transitions, typically 150–300ms, and avoid animating large layout areas unnecessarily.

Support `prefers-reduced-motion`.

Provide a global animation setting:
- Full.
- Reduced.
- Off.

When animation is disabled, preserve instant and accessible state changes.

Do not overuse parallax, bouncing, spinning, or continuous background animations.

